-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/711505e7-e10a-4b36-a299-3319ba4fdf83
-- title:
--   Theorem 3.5 — alternation: duality gap $\le$ (both regrets $+\sum\theta_{t+1}(F(x_{t+1},y_t)-F(x_t,y_t)))/S_T$ (corrected: $\theta_{t+1}$ inside the sum)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal X\subset\mathbb R^n$ and $\mathcal Y\subset\mathbb R^m$ be nonempty convex compact sets and $F:\mathcal X\times\mathcal Y\to\mathbb R$ convex in $x$ and concave in $y$. Let $T\ge1$, let $\theta_2,\dots,\theta_{T+1}>0$ be weights and $S_T=\sum_{t=1}^T\theta_{t+1}$. Let $x_1,\dots,x_{T+1}\in\mathcal X$ and $y_1,\dots,y_T\in\mathcal Y$, with losses as in the repeated game framework with alternation: $f_t\in\partial_xF(x_t,y_t)$ and $g_t\in\partial_yF(x_{t+1},y_t)$ (the second player sees $x_{t+1}$ before its update). Let
--
--   $$
--   (\bar x_T,\bar y_T)=\frac1{S_T}\sum_{t=1}^T\theta_{t+1}\,(x_{t+1},y_t).
--   $$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   \max_{y\in\mathcal Y}F(\bar x_T,y)-\min_{x\in\mathcal X}F(x,\bar y_T)\ \le\ &\frac1{S_T}\Big(\max_{y\in\mathcal Y}\sum_{t=1}^T\theta_{t+1}\langle g_t,y\rangle-\sum_{t=1}^T\theta_{t+1}\langle g_t,y_t\rangle\Big)\\
--   &+\frac1{S_T}\Big(\sum_{t=1}^T\theta_{t+1}\langle f_t,x_t\rangle-\min_{x\in\mathcal X}\sum_{t=1}^T\theta_{t+1}\langle f_t,x\rangle\Big)\\
--   &+\frac1{S_T}\sum_{t=1}^T\theta_{t+1}\big(F(x_{t+1},y_t)-F(x_t,y_t)\big).
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   The first two terms are the weighted regrets of the two players; the third measures how much the first player's own next decision improves on its current one against $y_t$. Alternation therefore converges to a saddle point whenever the third term is nonpositive, which Theorem 3.6 establishes for CBA and CBA$^+$ when $F$ is linear in $x$.
--
--   The page prints the first term as $\max_{y\in\mathcal Y}\theta_{t+1}\sum_{t=1}^T\langle g_t,y\rangle$, with $\theta_{t+1}$ outside the sum that binds $t$; the proof (Appendix C, p.24) derives the term from $\max_y\sum_t\theta_{t+1}F(x_{t+1},y)$, so the weight belongs inside the sum.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Stated for arbitrary decisions and (super)gradients at the points the alternating framework uses, so it covers every pair of algorithms, not only CBA and CBA$^+$. Subgradients are relative to $\mathcal X$ and $\mathcal Y$ (`BubeckCO.PSGD.IsSubgradient`; the supergradient $g_t$ as a subgradient $-g_t$ of $-F(x_{t+1},\cdot)$). The max and min of $F$ are suprema and infima of images (bounded under the hypotheses). The second term is `weightedRegret X (θ_{·+1}) f x T`.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - correction: max_{y∈Y} θ_{t+1} Σ_{t=1}^T ⟨g_t, y⟩ (θ_{t+1} outside the sum binding t) → max_{y∈Y} Σ_{t=1}^T θ_{t+1}⟨g_t, y⟩; reason: notation slip: the printed term has a free t; the proof (p.24) obtains it from max_y Σ_t θ_{t+1} F(x_{t+1}, y) and the supergradient inequality, which gives the weight inside the sum
--   - generalization: (x_t), (y_t) generated by the repeated game framework with alternation → arbitrary x_1, …, x_{T+1} ∈ X, y_1, …, y_T ∈ Y with f_t ∈ ∂_xF(x_t, y_t), g_t ∈ ∂_yF(x_{t+1}, y_t); reason: the framework fixes only where the (super)gradients are taken, which is all the theorem uses; every alternating run is an instance
--   - generalization: F subdifferentiable on X × Y → only the (super)gradients at the points above are assumed to exist; reason: no other subgradient is used; every subdifferentiable F supplies them
--   - reading: weights (θ_t)_{t≥1} → 0 < θ (t + 1) for 1 ≤ t ≤ T; reason: the paper's weights are positive; only θ_2, …, θ_{T+1} enter the statement, and S_T > 0 is needed for the averages
--   - encoding: max_{y∈Y} F(x̄_T, y), min_{x∈X} F(x, ȳ_T), and the max/min of the linear regret terms → sSup/sInf of images (weightedRegret for the x-term); reason: the F-images are nonempty and bounded under the hypotheses, the linear ones are attained on nonempty compact sets
--   - encoding: ∂_xF(x_t, y_t), ∂_yF(x_{t+1}, y_t) → IsSubgradient X (F(·, y_t)) x_t f_t and IsSubgradient Y (−F(x_{t+1}, ·)) y_t (−g_t), plus x_{t+1} ∈ X; reason: subgradients relative to X and Y; x_{t+1} ∈ X is the framework's x_{t+1} ∈ X
--   - encoding: ℝⁿ, ℝᵐ and rounds → E n, E m and sequences ℕ → · read on Finset.Icc 1 T; reason: Lean convention; same instances
-- source:
--   Grand-Clément & Kroer, Solving Optimization Problems with Blackwell Approachability, arXiv:2202.12277v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.12277v1), Theorem 3.5, p.11 (alternating framework, p.11; proof, Appendix C, p.24)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ApproachRegret_ToOLO_Cones
import Definitions.Def_BubeckCO_PSGD_IsSubgradient
import Definitions.Def_ConicBlackwell_weightedRegret
open scoped RealInnerProductSpace
open ApproachRegret.ToOLO

namespace ConicBlackwell.Supplement

/-- **Theorem 3.5**, Grand-Clément & Kroer, arXiv:2202.12277v1, p.11 (proof in Appendix C, p.24).
Consider weights `(θ_t)_{t≥1}`, `S_T = Σ_{t=1}^T θ_{t+1}`, and
`(x̄_T, ȳ_T) = Σ_{t=1}^T θ_{t+1} (x_{t+1}, y_t) / S_T`, where `f_t ∈ ∂_xF(x_t, y_t)` and
`g_t ∈ ∂_yF(x_{t+1}, y_t)` as in the repeated game framework with alternation.  Then
`max_{y∈Y} F(x̄_T, y) − min_{x∈X} F(x, ȳ_T)
   ≤ (1/S_T)(max_{y∈Y} Σ_t θ_{t+1}⟨g_t, y⟩ − Σ_t θ_{t+1}⟨g_t, y_t⟩)
   + (1/S_T)(Σ_t θ_{t+1}⟨f_t, x_t⟩ − min_{x∈X} Σ_t θ_{t+1}⟨f_t, x⟩)
   + (1/S_T)(Σ_t θ_{t+1}(F(x_{t+1}, y_t) − F(x_t, y_t)))`.

The page prints the first term as `max_{y∈Y} θ_{t+1} Σ_{t=1}^T ⟨g_t, y⟩`, with `θ_{t+1}` outside the
sum that binds `t`; the proof (p.24) derives it from `max_y Σ_t θ_{t+1}F(x_{t+1}, y)`, so the
weight belongs inside the sum, as stated here.

Formalization Note: stated for arbitrary decisions `x_1, …, x_{T+1} ∈ X`, `y_1, …, y_T ∈ Y` and
(super)gradients at the points the alternating framework uses (any algorithm, not only CBA/CBA+).
`F` is a function on `E n × E m` whose values off `X × Y` are never read; convex-concave as
`ConvexOn`/`ConcaveOn`; `f_t ∈ ∂_xF(x_t, y_t)` is `BubeckCO.PSGD.IsSubgradient` relative to `X`;
`g_t ∈ ∂_yF(x_{t+1}, y_t)` is `IsSubgradient Y (−F(x_{t+1}, ·)) y_t (−g_t)`.  Only the weights
`θ_2, …, θ_{T+1}` enter and they are assumed positive.  The max/min of `F` are `sSup`/`sInf` of
images (bounded under these hypotheses); the x-player's term is
`weightedRegret X (θ_{·+1}) f x T`. -/
theorem theorem_3_5 {n m : ℕ} (X : Set (E n)) (Y : Set (E m))
    (hXne : X.Nonempty) (hXc : IsCompact X) (hXcv : Convex ℝ X)
    (hYne : Y.Nonempty) (hYc : IsCompact Y) (hYcv : Convex ℝ Y)
    (F : E n → E m → ℝ)
    (hFx : ∀ y' ∈ Y, ConvexOn ℝ X (fun x' => F x' y'))
    (hFy : ∀ x' ∈ X, ConcaveOn ℝ Y (fun y' => F x' y'))
    (θ : ℕ → ℝ) (x : ℕ → E n) (y : ℕ → E m) (f : ℕ → E n) (g : ℕ → E m) (T : ℕ) (hT : 1 ≤ T)
    (hθ : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, 0 < θ (t + 1))
    (hx : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, x (t + 1) ∈ X)
    (hf : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
      BubeckCO.PSGD.IsSubgradient X (fun x' => F x' (y t)) (x t) (f t))
    (hg : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T,
      BubeckCO.PSGD.IsSubgradient Y (fun y' => -F (x (t + 1)) y') (y t) (-g t)) :
    sSup ((fun y' => F ((∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1))⁻¹ •
              ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1) • x (t + 1)) y') '' Y)
        - sInf ((fun x' => F x' ((∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1))⁻¹ •
              ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1) • y t)) '' X) ≤
      (1 / ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1)) *
          (sSup ((fun y' => ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1) * ⟪g t, y'⟫) '' Y)
            - ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1) * ⟪g t, y t⟫)
        + (1 / ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1)) * weightedRegret X (fun t => θ (t + 1)) f x T
        + (1 / ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1)) *
            ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, θ (t + 1) * (F (x (t + 1)) (y t) - F (x t) (y t)) := by sorry

end ConicBlackwell.Supplement
